Look up motors in the bundled catalog, read a .eng or .rse motor file, fetch a curve from ThrustCurve.org, or search vendors' stock and prices

Usage: hpr motors [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list    List the bundled catalog's motors, with the figures their curve files give
  show    Work out a motor's figures from its thrust curve: a catalog name, or a .eng or .rse file
  search  Search motor.fusionspace.co's motors, with who has them in stock and at what price
  fetch   Fetch a motor's thrust curve from ThrustCurve.org into the cache, so `hpr sim` flies it offline
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json
          Print one JSON document on standard output instead of text; errors too

      --color <WHEN>
          When to use color. Auto colors what goes to a terminal and heeds NO_COLOR, FORCE_COLOR and CLICOLOR_FORCE. JSON output never has color
          
          [default: auto]
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Examples:
  List the catalog's 38 mm H motors:
      hpr motors list --class H --diameter 38
  Work out a motor's figures from its thrust curve:
      hpr motors show H170M
  Find an L motor in stock:
      hpr motors search --class L --in-stock

Guide: https://hpr.fusionspace.co/cli.html#hpr-motors
